course: dictionary
lesson: 10647
title: Uninhabited
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Uninhabited is a long word, but you can break it into parts. Un- at the start means not, and inhabit means to live in a place. So uninhabited means not lived in. The context helps too: «He lives on an uninhabited island on the shores of the Red Sea.» An island on the shore where nobody lives is the same as an uninhabited island.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «He lives on an island where nobody lives» still makes sense, so you have the right meaning. This is the check you can use with any new word.
explain: Uninhabited is most often used for islands, deserts, planets or houses. It tells the reader that a place is empty, lonely or wild. An uninhabited house is a house with nobody living in it.
explain: Less often, uninhabited can mean that no animals or living things live in a place at all. When you meet the word, read the sentence around it and ask which meaning fits best.
fact: Un- at the start of a word means not.
fact: Inhabit means to live in a place, so uninhabited means not lived in.
fact: «Uninhabited» means with no people living there.
fact: Less often, «uninhabited» means with no animals or living things living there.
fact: Phrases you may see: «an uninhabited island» and «an uninhabited house».
exercise: «The explorers landed on an uninhabited island.» What does uninhabited mean? | Covered in snow all year | Full of tall buildings | *With no people living there | With many people shopping there
exercise: Which place is most likely to be uninhabited? | A school playground at break time | A crowded football stadium | A busy city centre | *A desert with no homes or villages
exercise: Which part of uninhabited means not? | inhabit | *un- | habit | -ited
test: «An uninhabited house has been empty for years.» What does uninhabited mean here? | It is made of wood | *Nobody lives in it | Somebody is painting it | It is very tall
test: Which word means the opposite of uninhabited? | Noisy | Frozen | Hidden | *Inhabited
exam: «He lives on an uninhabited island on the shores of the Red Sea.» What does this sentence tell us about the island? | It is hidden under the sea | It is in the middle of a big city | *Nobody else lives on it | It is full of shops and homes
